IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg11-s388-domestication`
IMPORT `dg11-s389-temporary-transfer`
IMPORT `dg11-s390-transfer-out`
IMPORT `dg11-s391-fees`
IMPORT `dg11-s393-s398-miscellaneous`
IMPORT `dg11-s395-trust-in-name`
IMPORT `dg11-seat`

-- Worked cases for the seat layer dg11-seat.l4: at least one case for every question, with the facts a real person in the seat would state.
-- Every expected value is worked by hand from the text of the section (the line is named beside it) and is not copied from the output of the rules.
-- The seat is a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation. The persons below are made up.

§ `Section 388 - Priya's family business becomes a Delaware corporation`

-- Priya, a director, and her brother Dev, a minority holder, own a limited liability company formed in a foreign country. They approved the domestication under its governing document before the certificate took effect, with the
-- certificate of incorporation approved by the same vote; both certificates were signed and filed together, to take effect on filing. src:1941-1944, 1956. Answer: yes.
#ASSERT `s 388(b) May my entity become domesticated as a Delaware corporation` `an entity that is a limited liability company` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Their lawyer files the certificate of incorporation a day after the certificate of corporate domestication: "filed simultaneously" fails. Answer: no.
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(b) May my entity become domesticated as a Delaware corporation` `an entity that is a limited liability company` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Their cousin, a natural person, asks the same. src:1940: an individual is not an entity. Answer: no.
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(b) May my entity become domesticated as a Delaware corporation` `a natural person, who is not an entity` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE

-- A statutory trust formed abroad is a non-United States entity (src:1940); an LLC formed in Delaware is not.
#ASSERT `s 388(a)(2) Is my entity a non-United States entity` `an entity that is a statutory trust` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(a)(2) Is my entity a non-United States entity` `an entity that is a limited liability company` `this State`

-- Priya is authorized to sign for the entity (src:1955); her cousin is not.
#ASSERT `s 388(g) May I sign the certificate of corporate domestication` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(g) May I sign the certificate of corporate domestication` FALSE

-- Approval (src:1956): given the right way, before the certificate took effect, certificate of incorporation approved by the same authorization: yes; approved only after the certificate took effect: no.
#ASSERT `s 388(h) Has the domestication of my entity been approved as required` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(h) Has the domestication of my entity been approved as required` TRUE FALSE TRUE

-- The certificate (src:1945-1951): items (1) to (5) given, no plan adopted: complete. With a plan adopted, (6) is also needed.
#ASSERT `s 388(c) Does my certificate of corporate domestication say everything required` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(c) Does my certificate of corporate domestication say everything required` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE

-- Both certificates are effective: the entity is a Delaware corporation (src:1952); its existence runs from 23 April 2012, when it first came into being abroad.
#ASSERT `s 388(d) Has my entity become a Delaware corporation` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(d) Has my entity become a Delaware corporation` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 388(d) From what date does my corporation's existence run` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2012 4 23) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2012 4 23)
#ASSERT `s 388(d) From what date does my corporation's existence run` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2012 4 23) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Dev owes a supplier for goods bought before the domestication: unaffected (src:1953).
#ASSERT `s 388(e) Does the domestication leave my obligation or liability alone` `an obligation or liability of the non-United States entity incurred prior to its domestication as a corporation in this State` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(e) Does the domestication leave my obligation or liability alone` `another matter that s 388(e) does not name` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Before the effective time the old choice of law stands; from it, Delaware law applies (src:1954).
#ASSERT `s 388(f) Which law applies to my entity` FALSE EQUALS `the choice of law that applied to it before the filing, unaffected by the filing`
#ASSERT `s 388(f) Which law applies to my entity` TRUE EQUALS `the law of the State of Delaware, including this title, as if it had been incorporated as a corporation of this State on that date`

-- After the domestication (src:1957): same entity; the entity still exists abroad, so the rights are held by the corporation and also the entity.
#ASSERT `s 388(i) Is the corporation the same entity as my entity` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(i) In whom do my entity's rights and property remain vested` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the corporation and also the non-United States entity, if and for so long as it continues its existence in the foreign jurisdiction in which it was existing immediately prior to the domestication`
#ASSERT `s 388(i) In whom do my entity's rights and property remain vested` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the corporation alone`
#ASSERT `s 388(i) To whom do my entity's debts and liabilities remain attached` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the corporation alone`
#ASSERT `s 388(i) Is my entity's title to real property impaired` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Marta, a supplier owed money by the entity, keeps her rights and liens.
#ASSERT `s 388(i) Are my creditor's rights and liens preserved` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(i) Does the domestication count as a transfer` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The entity need not wind up unless otherwise agreed or required (src:1958); and the domestication is not a dissolution.
#ASSERT `s 388(j) Must my entity wind up` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 388(j) Must my entity wind up` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 388(j) Is the domestication a dissolution of my entity` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 388(j) Do my entity and the corporation count as a single entity` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Dev's units in the entity may be cancelled in the domestication (src:1959); a treatment the subsection does not name is not covered.
#ASSERT `s 388(k) Can my shares or interests be so treated` `cancelled in a domestication` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(k) Can my shares or interests be so treated` `treated in a way that s 388(k) does not name` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The plan (src:1960).
#ASSERT `s 388(l) May the plan of domestication state it` `the mode of carrying the same into effect` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(l) May a term of the plan depend on facts outside the plan` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(l) May a term of the plan depend on facts outside the plan` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 388(l)(v) May the corporation take the action stated in the plan` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(l) May a term of the plan depend on this kind of fact` `a determination or action by any person or body, including the non-United States entity or the domesticated corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(l) May a term of the plan depend on this kind of fact` `a fact of another kind that s 388(l) does not name` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(l)(v) May the corporation take the action stated in the plan` FALSE
-- A corporate action in an approved plan, within the powers of a corporation, needs no further board or stockholder action (src:1961).
#ASSERT `s 388(m) Is the action deemed approved with no further action` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 388(m) Is the action deemed approved with no further action` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `s 388(m) Does my certificate carry the required statement` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 388(m) Does my certificate carry the required statement` TRUE TRUE

§ `Section 389 - Tomas's company moves its domicile into Delaware during a war`

-- Tomas is a director of a company governed by the law of a country at war. src:1967: war is an emergency condition.
#ASSERT `s 389(a)(1) Is this event an emergency condition` `war or other armed conflict` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(a)(1) Is this event an emergency condition` `such other event which, under the law of the jurisdiction governing the internal affairs of the non-United States entity, permits the non-United States entity to transfer its domicile` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(a)(1) Is this event an emergency condition` `another event that s 389(a)(1) does not list` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Tomas is a trustee and manager, not formally a director: still counts (src:1978).
#ASSERT `s 389(a)(3) Do I count as an officer or a director` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(a)(3) Do I count as an officer or a director` FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The company is an LLC formed abroad, has complied, and its law does not prohibit the transfer (src:1979): yes. If its law expressly prohibits it: no.
#ASSERT `s 389(b) May my entity transfer its domicile into Delaware` `an entity that is a limited liability company` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(b) May my entity transfer its domicile into Delaware` `an entity that is a limited liability company` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(b) Does moving this place count as moving my domicile` `the principal place of business of the entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(b) Does moving this place count as moving my domicile` `a place of another kind that s 389(b) does not name` EQUALS NOTHING

-- The company submitted its documents on 1 June 2026 for a transfer proposed for 1 July 2026: 30 days before (src:1980). In time. A day later: too late unless the Secretary of State waives.
#ASSERT `s 389(c) Did my entity submit its documents in time` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) Did my entity submit its documents in time` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 2) (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) FALSE
#ASSERT `s 389(c) Did my entity submit its documents in time` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 2) (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) TRUE
-- Everything submitted with the $10,000 examination fee, the (c)(4) certificate complete, all documents in English (src:1981-1992): satisfies. Fee $9,999.99: does not.
#ASSERT `s 389(c) Do my entity's documents satisfy section 389` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 10_000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) Do my entity's documents satisfy section 389` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 9_999.99 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 389(c) Is the translation requirement met` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) Is the translation requirement met` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 389(c) Must the Secretary of State tell my entity its documents are accepted` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) Must the Secretary of State tell my entity its documents are accepted` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 389(c) Is my entity's name on the reserved list` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) Is my entity's name on the reserved list` FALSE TRUE
-- Nobody may inspect the documents under Chapter 100 of Title 29 until the entity transfers (src:1992); afterwards the sentence says nothing.
#ASSERT `s 389(c) Can others inspect my entity's documents` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 389(c) Can others inspect my entity's documents` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 389(c) May the Secretary of State waive the 30-day period and the translation requirement` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(c) May the Secretary of State waive the 30-day period and the translation requirement` TRUE FALSE

-- The annual certificate (src:1993).
#ASSERT `s 389(d) Must my entity file the annual certificate` `during the transfer of its domicile` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(d) Must my entity file the annual certificate` `after its domicile has ceased to be in this State, and it does not desire to continue to be subject to a transfer of domicile under this section` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 389(d) By what date must my entity file the annual certificate` 2027 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 3 1
#ASSERT `s 389(d) Is my entity's annual certificate in order` TRUE TRUE 2_500
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(d) Is my entity's annual certificate in order` TRUE TRUE 2_499.99
-- Filed on 1 March 2027: in time. Not filed by 2 March 2027: void from that day. Filed on 2 March: too late.
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(d) Have my entity's certificates and filings become void` 2027 TRUE (YearMonthDay 2027 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2027 3 2)
#ASSERT `s 389(d) Have my entity's certificates and filings become void` 2027 FALSE (YearMonthDay 2027 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2027 3 2)
#ASSERT `s 389(d) Have my entity's certificates and filings become void` 2027 TRUE (YearMonthDay 2027 3 2) (YearMonthDay 2027 3 9)
#ASSERT `s 389(d) Must my entity start again with all the submissions and the examination fee` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(d) Must my entity start again with all the submissions and the examination fee` FALSE

-- Making the transfer (src:1994): accepted documents, a signed written communication confirming the statements, by ordinary means: valid.
#ASSERT `s 389(e) Has my entity validly transferred its domicile` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1)
-- By telegram because emergency conditions cut the ordinary means; the signed duplicate arrived on 31 July (30 days after 1 July): valid. On 1 August: not.
#ASSERT `s 389(e) Has my entity validly transferred its domicile` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 7 31)
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(e) Has my entity validly transferred its domicile` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 8 1)
#ASSERT `s 389(e) Must the Secretary of State record the transfer` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(e) Must the Secretary of State certify that my entity has filed and paid everything` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(e) Is the Secretary of State's certificate prima facie evidence of the transfer` TRUE

-- After the transfer (src:1995-1997).
#ASSERT `s 389(f) Does my entity keep the power it had` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(f) Does my entity keep the power it had` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 389(f) May I manage my entity under the law governing its internal affairs` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(f) Is my entity treated as doing business in Delaware` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 389(f) Which version of the foreign law is meant` TRUE EQUALS JUST `the law as in effect immediately prior to the transfer of domicile`
#ASSERT `s 389(g) Can my entity be treated as an enemy` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 389(h) Does the transfer leave my entity's earlier obligation alone` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Dividends (src:1998): the directors may withhold a holder's dividend if they find she will not have the full benefit and they provide an escrow. Ada, a minority holder, is told her dividend is held in escrow: lawful.
#ASSERT `s 389(i) May the directors withhold my dividend` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(i) May the directors withhold my dividend` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 389(i) May I as a director withhold the amount` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(i) May I as a director withhold the amount` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- Service (src:1999).
#ASSERT `s 389(j) Can process be served on my entity as on a Delaware corporation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(j) Have I done what is required before taking office` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(j) Have I done what is required before taking office` TRUE FALSE
-- Withdrawal (src:2000).
#ASSERT `s 389(k) Is my entity's application to withdraw complete` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(k) Is my entity's application to withdraw complete` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 389(k) Must the Secretary of State file my entity's application` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(k) Must the Secretary of State file my entity's application` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 389(k) Has my entity's domicile ceased to be in Delaware` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 389(k) Has my entity's domicile ceased to be in Delaware` FALSE TRUE

§ `Section 390 - Chen's Delaware corporation moves to a foreign jurisdiction`

-- Chen is a director of a Delaware corporation that wants to continue in a foreign jurisdiction while keeping its Delaware existence; Lena holds 40% of the stock; Omar is a stockholder who will become a general partner.
#ASSERT `s 390(a)(1) Is this place a foreign jurisdiction` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(a)(1) Is this place a foreign jurisdiction` `another jurisdiction of the United States`
-- src:2004: a Delaware corporation, going to a foreign jurisdiction, with the resolution, the vote and the certificate: may.
#ASSERT `s 390(a) May my corporation move out of Delaware` TRUE `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(a) May my corporation move out of Delaware` TRUE `another jurisdiction of the United States` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(b) Which certificate must my corporation file` TRUE EQUALS `a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance`
#ASSERT `s 390(b) Which certificate must my corporation file` FALSE EQUALS `a certificate of transfer`
-- src:2007: resolution adopted, names the jurisdiction, states continued existence, recommends, plan approved together.
#ASSERT `s 390(b) Has the board adopted the resolution as required` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b) Has the board adopted the resolution as required` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Notice: Lena was sent notice on 10 June 2026 for a meeting on 30 June 2026: 20 days before: in time. On 11 June: not.
#ASSERT `s 390(b) Was the notice of the meeting given as required` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b) Was the notice of the meeting given as required` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 11) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b) Was the notice of the meeting given as required` TRUE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30)
-- Vote: 51 of 100 votes carries; exactly 50 does not. As a partnership with 2 general partners among the stockholders: both must approve.
#ASSERT `s 390(b) Have the stockholders adopted the resolution` 51 100 FALSE 0 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(b) Have the stockholders adopted the resolution` 50 100 FALSE 0 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 390(b) Have the stockholders adopted the resolution` 51 100 TRUE 2 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 390(b) Have the stockholders adopted the resolution` 101 100 FALSE 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Omar will become a general partner: his own approval is required. Lena will not: hers is not.
#ASSERT `s 390(b) Must I approve the move myself` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b) Must I approve the move myself` TRUE FALSE
-- The certificate of transfer and domestic continuance: (1) to (4) and (6); and (7) if a plan is adopted.
#ASSERT `s 390(b) Does my corporation's certificate certify everything required` `a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b) Does my corporation's certificate certify everything required` `a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 390(b) Does my corporation's certificate certify everything required` `a certificate of transfer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Service of process on a corporation that has transferred out (src:2012). Fatima is suing it.
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b)(5) Is the address given for the mailing of process permitted` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) Is the address given for the mailing of process permitted` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) May process be served by electronic transmission` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) To what address will the Secretary of State mail the letter` "1 Main Street" FALSE "unused" EQUALS "1 Main Street"
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) To what address will the Secretary of State mail the letter` "1 Main Street" TRUE "2 Oak Avenue" EQUALS "2 Oak Avenue"
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) Was the letter sent as required` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b)(5) Was the letter sent as required` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) How much must I pay the Secretary of State on service` EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) Have I done what the plaintiff's duty on service requires` TRUE TRUE 50
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(b)(5) Have I done what the plaintiff's duty on service requires` TRUE TRUE 40
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) Is the sum I paid taxed as part of the costs` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) Is the sum I paid taxed as part of the costs` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) Is the Secretary of State still required to keep the record` 5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(b)(5) Is the Secretary of State still required to keep the record` 6 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- After filing a certificate of transfer (src:2015).
#ASSERT `s 390(c) Must the Secretary of State certify that my corporation has filed and paid everything` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(c) Has my corporation ceased to exist in Delaware` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(c) Has my corporation ceased to exist in Delaware` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 390(c) Is the Secretary of State's certificate prima facie evidence of the move` TRUE
-- src:2016.
#ASSERT `s 390(d) Does the move leave my earlier obligation or liability alone` `the personal liability of a person incurred prior to the transfer, domestication or continuance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(d) Must my corporation wind up` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 390(d) Must my corporation wind up` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 390(d) Is the move a dissolution of my corporation` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:2017.
#ASSERT `s 390(e) Does my corporation continue to exist in Delaware` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(e) Does my corporation continue to exist in Delaware` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 390(e) Are the continuing corporation and the resulting entity a single entity` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- src:2018: Lena's shares and Fatima's judgment debt are against the resulting entity (and the corporation, as it continues in Delaware).
#ASSERT `s 390(f) Is the resulting entity the same entity as my corporation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(f) In whom do my corporation's rights and property remain vested` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the resulting entity and also the corporation, for so long as the corporation continues its existence as a corporation of this State`
#ASSERT `s 390(f) To whom do my corporation's debts remain attached` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the resulting entity alone`
#ASSERT `s 390(f) Is my corporation's title to real property impaired by the move` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 390(f) Are my creditor's rights and liens preserved after the move` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(f) Does the move count as a transfer to the resulting entity` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Lena's shares may be converted into shares of the resulting entity (src:2019).
#ASSERT `s 390(g) Can my shares be so treated in the move` `exchanged for or converted into shares of stock, rights or securities of, or interests in, the resulting entity in a transfer, domestication or continuance` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No stock has been issued yet (src:2020): no vote needed. If shares were issued: needed.
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(h) Is a stockholder vote necessary for the move` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 390(h) Is a stockholder vote necessary for the move` TRUE
-- Nonstock (src:2021).
#ASSERT `s 390(i) Does the governing body perform the board's acts` `a charitable nonstock corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(i) Does the governing body perform the board's acts` `a stock corporation` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 390(i) Who authorizes the move of a nonstock corporation` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the members entitled to vote, and any other holder of a membership interest`
#ASSERT `s 390(i) Who authorizes the move of a nonstock corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the governing body at a meeting, by a majority of its members then in office`
#ASSERT `s 390(i) Has the governing body authorized the move by a majority` 5 9 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(i) Has the governing body authorized the move by a majority` 4 9 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 390(i) Must the proceedings conform to those for a corporation with capital stock` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(i) Must my corporation mail notice to the Attorney General` `a charitable nonstock corporation`
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(i) Must my corporation mail notice to the Attorney General` `a stock corporation`
#ASSERT `s 390(i) Was the notice to the Attorney General mailed in time` (YearMonthDay 2026 9 20) (YearMonthDay 2026 9 30)
#ASSERT NOT `s 390(i) Was the notice to the Attorney General mailed in time` (YearMonthDay 2026 9 21) (YearMonthDay 2026 9 30)
-- The plan (src:2022).
#ASSERT `s 390(j) May the plan state it` `any details or provisions as are deemed desirable` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(j) May a term of the plan depend on facts outside the plan` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(j) May a term of the plan depend on this kind of fact` `the occurrence of any event` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 390(j) May a term of the plan depend on this kind of fact` `a fact of another kind that s 390(j) does not name` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Merger restrictions (src:2023): Lena's stockholders' agreement came into effect on 1 August 2023 ("on or before"): its merger restriction applies to the move as if it were a merger.
#ASSERT `s 390(k) Does the merger restriction also apply to a move out` `in a voting trust agreement or other written agreement between or among the corporation and 1 or more of its stockholders (s 390(k))` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2023 8 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `as if the transfer, domestication or continuance were a merger or consolidation`
-- The certificate of incorporation of a corporation incorporated on 1 August 2023 is not "before" that date: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 390(k) Does the merger restriction also apply to a move out` `in the certificate of incorporation of the corporation (s 390(k))` (YearMonthDay 2023 8 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 391 - Nadia's startup files with the Secretary of State`

-- Nadia incorporates a startup with 100,000,000 shares of $0.001 par value: $100,000 of authorized capital stock, so 1,000 assessable shares at $0.02 each (src:2029) = $20.00.
#ASSERT `s 391(a)(1) What fee must I pay to file an original certificate of incorporation` 100_000_000 0.001 0 EQUALS 20
-- A smaller startup with 5,000,000 shares of $0.001 par value: 50 assessable shares, $1.00, so the $15 floor applies.
#ASSERT `s 391(a)(1) What fee must I pay to file an original certificate of incorporation` 5_000_000 0.001 0 EQUALS 15
-- Paragraph (a)(7): a certificate of incorporation filed under section 102 adds $25 and $5 (src:2040); a paper with no different fee adds $115 and $5.
#ASSERT `s 391(a)(7) What fees does paragraph (a)(7) lay on my instrument` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `s 391(a)(7) What fees does paragraph (a)(7) lay on my instrument` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 120
-- An amendment raising the authorized shares from 1,000,000 to 3,000,000 of $1 par value (10,000 to 30,000 assessable shares: $500 less $200 = $300, src:2030, 2066).
#ASSERT `s 391(b)(2) Does my certificate count as increasing the authorized capital stock` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 3_000_000 1 0 1_000_000 1 0
#ASSERT `s 391(a)(2) or (3) What fee must I pay to file my amendment or restated certificate` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 3_000_000 1 0 1_000_000 1 0 FALSE EQUALS 300
-- A name change that leaves the capital alone: $30 (src:2031); an exempt corporation pays nothing under that paragraph.
#ASSERT `s 391(a)(2) or (3) What fee must I pay to file my amendment or restated certificate` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1_000_000 1 0 1_000_000 1 0 FALSE EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `s 391(a)(2) or (3) What fee must I pay to file my amendment or restated certificate` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1_000_000 1 0 1_000_000 1 0 TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 391(a)(3) What fee must I pay to file any other certificate` FALSE EQUALS 5
-- A merger of two corporations of $2,000,000 of par stock together into one of $5,000,000: $700 less $400 = $300 (src:2032); with $25.50 of another law's fee for a constituent that is not a corporation: $325.50.
#ASSERT `s 391(a)(4) What fee must I pay to file a certificate of merger or consolidation` 5_000_000 1 0 2_000_000 0 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `s 391(a)(4) What is the total payable with another law's tax or fee` 300 25.50 EQUALS 325.5
-- Dissolution (src:2033-2038): a clean certificate $50; one lacking a certification $40.
#ASSERT `s 391(a)(5) What fee must I pay to file a certificate of dissolution` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `s 391(a)(5) What fee must I pay to file a certificate of dissolution` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 40
-- Flat fees (src:2039-2064).
#ASSERT `s 391(a) What is the most I can be charged for this paper or service` `the annual report of a foreign corporation doing business in this State (s 391(a)(8))` EQUALS 250
#ASSERT `s 391(a) What is the most I can be charged for this paper or service` `a certificate of transfer or a certificate of continuance prescribed in s 390 (s 391(a)(25))` EQUALS 1_000
